# Read at BUILD time to prerender the salon list into the page, and at RUNTIME
# by the waitlist form — the one network call this site makes from a browser,
# and only when somebody presses Join.
#
# The publishable (anon) key is safe to expose — Row-Level Security is the gate,
# and everything this site reads is anon-readable by policy: approved+active
# businesses, their services, the service catalogue, opening hours and reviews.
#
# The waitlist is the reverse shape and is worth understanding before changing
# it: `app_waitlist` has RLS enabled with NO policies and no table grants, so
# this key cannot read a single row of it. The only thing it can do is call
# `join_app_waitlist()`, a SECURITY DEFINER function that inserts and returns
# nothing but "joined" or "already". A visitor cannot enumerate the list they
# just joined.
#
# There is no service_role key here and there must never be one: this site
# renders public marketing content and nothing else.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://izlyevebmxqlxinigote.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_Ve9ENI8gAovucWDHRzKuRg_TaVW_Uhe

# Where the product lives — the tho_web app, a different origin from this site.
# The header's "Sign in" button is the only thing that reads it.
#
# Inlined at BUILD time (it is NEXT_PUBLIC_), so changing it needs a rebuild —
# not a redeploy of the same bundle. A trailing slash is stripped for you.
#
# Locally both apps run `next dev` on port 3000, so whichever starts second
# lands on 3001. If tho_web is the one on 3001, set that here and restart the
# dev server; the value is compiled into the client bundle.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
